    "narrative": "For July 4th, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into matchup exploitation, led by **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll**. **Brice Turang** earns the day's highest efficiency score (75.05) by drawing a favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly; with an xERA of 5.47, Kelly provides the optimal environment for **Brice Turang** to capitalize on his top-of-the-order production. **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start (73.47) not just for his expected output, but because his matchup against Brandon Woodruff\u2014who has a notably slow delivery\u2014offers high-upside potential for stolen bases, the scarcest currency in our 5x5 build. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (69.93) and **Kyle Karros** (63.19) benefit significantly from park factors and a favorable draw against Robbie Ray, whose vulnerability to high-impact contact pairs perfectly with their current hitting profiles.\n\nWhile our starting nine remains aggressive, the benching of **Austin Riley** (49.37) was the most difficult decision of the day. Despite his pedigree, **Austin Riley** narrowly missed the cut due to a challenging clash with Sean Manaea; the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of players like **Max Muncy** (61.13), whose park-adjusted upside against Sandy Alcantara outweighed the historical consistency of **Austin Riley**. Managers should note that **Travis Bazzana** (52.20) carries a weather-related risk, with a 37% chance of rain that could shorten his day despite his prime leadoff spot. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players, particularly **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency score of 57.65 relies heavily on our projected #8 spot; any movement higher or lower in the order will alter his contribution threshold significantly. With the rotation depth currently available, we are prepared to pivot if late-breaking reports suggest unfavorable weather or lineup shifts for **Travis Bazzana** or **Alex Freeland**.",
